-- title:
--   Each branch at a crossing is regular: 𝔪 = P+(t)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ (with $M/p \neq 0$), and assume the $q$-expansion $j =$ `jqModC ℚ` lies in the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios of integral forms for $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a bundle of Deligne–Rapoport properties `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for the model $X$ of level $\Gamma_H(M)$ over $R = R\,p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R \to A$ a ring map compatible with the structure map $R \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring with a ring map $\rho_O : R \to O$ such that the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by the image of $p$, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ a ring map with $\mathrm{to}\kappa \circ \rho_O$ equal to $\rho$ followed by the residue map of $A$; write $X_O$ for the base change `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, the pullback of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` along $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_O)$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho\,0$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho\,1$, and let $x_n$ be its image in $X_O$ under `pullback.fst` followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\dots 0$ followed by `bcMap (ΓM M H) hj ρO toκ htoκ`. Assume the points `𝔛.ξinf` and `𝔛.ξzero` of $X_O$ both specialise to $x_n$, with specialisation witnesses $h_\infty$, $h_0$. Then in the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{X_O, x_n}$ there exist elements $t$ and $t'$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{x_n} = P_\infty + (t)$ and $\mathfrak{m}_{x_n} = P_0 + (t')$, where $P_\infty$ and $P_0$ are the branch ideals of $h_\infty$ and $h_0$, that is the contractions of the maximal ideals of the stalks at `𝔛.ξinf`, resp. `𝔛.ξzero`, along the specialisation maps $\mathcal{O}_{X_O,x_n} \to \mathcal{O}_{X_O,\xi}$.
--
--   This is the local statement, at a crossing point of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ over a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$, that each of the two branches through the crossing is regular there: modulo the branch ideal the maximal ideal becomes principal. It feeds into [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_span_pair_baseGerm_eq_branchIdeal), where the two branch parameters are combined into a description of the local ring at a crossing.
